On Tue, 7 Mar 2000, Cirad wrote:

> I've got a big file with 28761 lines. I would like to build a sample
> data but I've got some trouble with the "sample" function.
> 
> I managed to build  a sample with the following code :
> 
> n <- nrow(surf4)
> echan <- sample(n,size=floor(n/4))
> surftest <- surf4[echan, ]
> 
> But it isn't what I want. I've got in my file 298 herds (variable "herd"
> 
> with values between 1-298) which have repeated measures (nearly 100
> measures by herd). I only would like to sample  this file, not on the
> 28761 lines but on the "herd" variable. So that I keep all the measures
> from a specific herd but I don't take all the herd in my sample.

Something like

samp <- sample(unique(surf4$herd), 50)
surf4[match(surf4$herd, samp, 0) > 0, ]

will take a random sample of 50 herds, which is what I understand you want.

