Dear Splus-Users

Earlier this morning I posted a question concerning a compiler error for
the ash-library of D. Scott.
I found a way to solve this problem. Possibly you are interested for the
solution. Just include more brackets in the assingement of the struct:

simpint.c:
#include <stdio.h>
struct connection {
        int n, start[5], end[5];
} C[5][5] = {
{{0},{3,{0,0,0},{1,2,3}},{4,{0,2,1,3},{2,1,3,0}},{3,{3,3,3},{0,1,2}},{0}},
{{0},{3,{0,0,1},{2,3,1}},{3,{0,1,2},{3,3,2}},{0},{0}},
{{0},{3,{0,1,2},{3,1,2}},{0},{0},{0}},
{{3,{0,1,2},{0,1,2}},{3,{1,2,3},{1,2,3}},{0},{0},{0}},
{{0},{0},{0},{0},{0}}
};
.......

Christoph

