Andy Liaw :

 If I understand you correctly, you want a random sample of "herds", but
the
data frame contains multiple records per herd.

Let me try it on a made-up data set:

dat<-data.frame(herd=sort(rep(1:298,length=28761)),x=rnorm(28761))
herd.sample<-sample(unique(dat$herd,floor(length(unique(dat$herd))/4))
dat.sample<-dat[is.element(dat$herd,herd.sample),]

dat.sample should give you want you want.  Hope this helps.

