I would like to thank Naomi Robbins, Luciano Molinari, Samantha Choy, Melanie 
Cox, Z. Todd Taylor, Anne York and Ronald Fehd for their replies. I ended up 
using the function that Anne York sent me. I have modified it somewhat and will 
post the modifed version latter. Here is the original form:

"Twoplots" <-
function(x1, y1, x2, y2, type = "l", xlim = NULL, ptitle = "Twoplots", xlab
= "x", ylab1 = "y1", ylab2 = "y2", ...)
{
# Written by AE York Sept. 1996
# Plots y1 vs x1 and y2 vs x2 on the same plot
# Labels for y1 are on the left and labels for y2 on the right
        oldpar <- par()
        par(mar = rep(6, 4))    #       
        if(missing(xlim))
                xlim <- range(pretty(range(c(x1, x2))))
        plot(x1, y1, lty = 1, pch = 1, type = type, xlim = xlim, xlab =
                xlab, ylab = ylab1, ...)
        par(new = T)
        plot(x2, y2, lty = 2, pch = 16, type = type, axes = F, xlim = xlim, 
                xlab = "", ylab = "")
        axis(side = 4)
        mtext(ylab2, side = 4, line = 2, outer = F)
        par(oldpar)
        title(ptitle)
}

