Thanks to all who responded to my query regarding copying (in a symmetric
matrix) the part below the diagonal onto the part above the diagonal.  I'm
always amazed at the speed, number and elegance of the responses from the
participants in S-news.

Below are the two recommended methods, each of which work quickly and easily.
I prefer the first of these, because the syntax seems most natural.

x[row(x) > col(x)] <- t(x)[row(x) > col(x)]
x[lower.tri(x,FALSE)] <- t(x)[lower.tri(x,FALSE)]

Cheers,
karl

