process).  I suggest you use your OS tools to look at the performance
statistics while your BATCH jobs are running.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

I did open a performance meter to look at the cpu usage while the jobs
are running and also used ps -aux to check. As speed slows down, the cpu
usage becomes much lower while the memory usage is pushed to limit. I've
run some jobs on a machine with larger memory and it gets better. I
haven't got time to run the same jobs in S-Plus3.4 for comparison.

