per aging time unit (days, in my case), as predicted by ordinary linear
regression.

The antilog of -0.210721 is 0.81.   But what similarly simple claim can I
make about the relationship of output to age as predicted by generalized
additive modeling?  Is output falling 19% per day?  Just what does this
parametric coefficient mean for a nonparametric term?

Any advice would be greatly appreciated.

