I have just been subsetting a number of data frames each containing several
factors with new.df <- old.df[factor1=="level",] (but not within a
function).

However, when using the Vary Symbols option for GUI 2D scatter plots I
experienced problems which appeared related to the fact that obsolete levels
of the factors in old.df are retained in new.df. I ended up using

new.df <- data.frame(as.matrix(old.df[factor1=="level",]))

to work around this, but one would think there ought to be a more efficient
way to deal with such cases.

