Subject: [S] Summary: Extracting non NULL elements of a list.
Message-ID: <852568AA.004DABEA.00@mail.spgdag.com>

Hello S-users,

Yesterday I posted a question about extracting non null elements from a list.
Thanks to Bill Dunlap, Samuel Buttrey, Peter Perkins, Matt Calder, Bill
Venables, Julian Taylor and Nick Ellis for their replies.  I basically
got for ways of doing it:

Samuel Buttrey:  ttt <- ttt[sapply (ttt, length) > 0]

Matt Calder, Julian Taylor and Nick Ellis: ttt[!sapply(ttt, is.null)]

Bill Venables: for (i in length(ttt):1) ttt[[i]] <- ttt[[i]]  # Note that the
loop starts from the end.

Bill Dunlap: ttt[!unlist(lapply(ttt, is.null))]

Bill Dunlap also mention the "sapply" solution but he suggests that it takes a
little longer to execute than the
"unlist(lapply...))" solution.

Thanks to all who responded, the original message follows,

