Many, many thanks for your replies.

> "Martin H. H. Stevens" wrote:
>
> > How do I get permenent row names after I tabulate an vector of integers?
>
> RESPONSE 1.
> If I understand you correctly, try the following:
>
> x<-1:10
> names(x)<-LETTERS[1:10]
> names(x)
>
> Andy Liaw
> Merck Biometrics Research
> Phone: (732) 594-0820
> Fax: (732) 594-1565
> mailto:andy_liaw at merck.com
>
> RESPONSE 2.
> It is understood with the use of tabulate, that you are
> tabulating positive
> integers. The length of the output vector in the maximum value of
> the
> vector that is tabulated.  So, if you say foo <- tabulate(x),then
> you could
> write foo <- data.frame(count.label=seq(along=foo),count=foo)
>
> tabulate does not always give you what you expect. Sometimes you
> need to
> use the function table. In that case, you could say
>
> foo <- data.frame(table(x)). Here the row names will be the
> values of x,
> which do not have to be positive integers.
>
