From macq at llnl.gov  Thu Mar 23 01:22:05 2000
From: macq at llnl.gov (Don MacQueen)
Date: Wed, 22 Mar 2000 17:22:05 -0800
Subject: [S] significant digits bug in Splus 5.1
Message-ID: <v0421010bb4ff1ebca762@[128.115.153.6]>

I have long believed that SPlus was the only software package in my 
possession that did significant digits correctly.

Today I discovered that while version 3.4 did, version 5.1 does not. 
MathSoft has introduced a bug in version 5.1. See below.

----- Version 5.1 -----

> version
Version 5.1 Release 1 for Sun SPARC, SunOS 5.5 : 1999
### these are correct
> signif(1.637,3)
[1] 1.64
> signif(1.637,2)
[1] 1.6
> signif(1.637,1)
[1] 2
### these are not correct
> signif(1637,3)
[1] 1637             ## correct result is 1640
> signif(1637,2)
[1] 1637             ## correct result is 1600
> signif(1637,1)
[1] 1637             ## correct result is 2000

----- Whereas in version 3.4 -----

> version
Version 3.4 Release 1 for Sun SPARC, SunOS 5.3 : 1996
> signif(1637,3)
[1] 1640
> signif(1637,2)
[1] 1600
> signif(1637,1)
[1] 2000
>

I apologize, sort of, for being critical, but this is an almost 
incomprehensible mistake. If it ain't broke, don't fix it. Obviously, 
the software testing process has been inadequate.

Because the function is .Internal, it is not easy for users to fix.
> signif
function(x, digits = 6.)
.Internal(signif(x, digits), "do_math", T, 130)

Is a patch available? If not, one should be made available ASAP.

Thank you,
-Don
