From gb at stat.umu.se  Thu Mar 23 07:48:39 2000
From: gb at stat.umu.se
Date: Thu, 23 Mar 2000 08:48:39 +0100
Subject: Re: [S] Exact bootstrap distribution for Bernoulli sequence
In-Reply-To: <38D98325.52676F41@virginia.edu>
References: <38D98325.52676F41@virginia.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.10.10003230843280.30956-100000@pc16.stat.umu.se>

Frank,

this is an easy one; since you draw with replacement, the draws are
(conditionally on s) independent. In each draw, p = s/(n-s) is
the probability of getting a one (still conditionally on s).
So, the resulting distribution of the number of ones is 
Binomial(n, p). (Since you condition on  s, the original 
distribution is irrelevant.)

Göran

