My thanks to Nicole DePriest, Bill Dunlap, Steve McKinney, Peter 
Perkins, Charles C. Berry. The workarounds are simple, and the bug 
will be fixed in the next version.

>From Bill Dunlap (MathSoft):

As a workaround, if you call signif with a floating point argument
instead of an integer it will work in 5.1.

        > signif(1637,3)
        [1] 1637
        >  signif(1637.,3)
        [1] 1640

Similarly, from MathSoft tech support, use as.numeric() or as.double():

> signif(as.numeric(1637), 3)
[1] 1640
> signif(as.double(1637), 3)
[1] 1640

